          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : E \to F
            between
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            of the underlying categories that is consistent with the interpretation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            as generalized
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo =
                  %mi Set
                  %mo =
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F = Set = Sh(*)
            is the terminal
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to Set
            is essential if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topos"} locally connected topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            being essential is a necessary (but not sufficient) condition to ensure that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            behaves like a map of topological spaces whose
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+geometric+morphism"} locally connected geometric morphism
          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo ⊣
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f^* \dashv f_*) : E \to F
              %strong essential geometric morphism
              if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
              functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
              has not only the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo !
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi E
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟵
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mo !
                    %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (f_! \dashv f^* \dashv f_*)
                    \\;\;\; : \;\;\;
                    E
                    \\stackrel{\overset{f_!}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{f^*}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{f_*}{\longrightarrow}}}
                    F
                    \\,.
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} point of a topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi Set
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x : Set \to E
            which is given by an essential geometric morphism is called an
            %strong essential point
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p There are various further conditions that can be imposed on a geometric morphism:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo !
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!
                  can be made into an
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+functor"} indexed functor
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
                  satisfies some extra conditions, the geometric morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+geometric+morphism"} locally connected geometric morphism
                  (see there for details).
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo !
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!
                  preserves finite
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
                  then
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is called
                  = succeed "." do
                    %strong connected surjective
              %li
                %p
                  If in addition to the above
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+geometric+morphism"} local geometric morphism
                  in that there is a further functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo !
                        %mo :
                        %mi F
                        %mo →
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^! : F \to E
                  which is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                        %mo ⊣
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo !
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f_* \dashv f^!)
                  and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful
                  then the geometric morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is called
                  = succeed "." do
                    %strong
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Since for a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^*
              of an essential point is of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_E(P,-)
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ≇
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\ncong\emptyset
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projective
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected"} connected
              %em essential objects
              (cf.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#JTT77"} Johnstone 1977, p.255
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#a_criterion_for_grothendieck_toposes A criterion for Grothendieck toposes
          %p
            The inverse image
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
            of an essential geometric morphism preserves small limits since it is a right adjoint. Hence, this provides a minimal requirement to satisfy for a general geometric morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast\dashv f_\ast
            in order to qualify for being essential. In case, the toposes involved are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+toposes"} Grothendieck toposes
            this condition is not only necessary but sufficient.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℱ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast\dashv f_\ast:\mathcal{E}\to\mathcal{F}
              a geometric morphism between Grothendieck toposes. Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is essential iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
              preserves small limits iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
              preserves small products.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Grothendieck toposes are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
              has rank i.e. it preserves
              = succeed "-filtered" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              since it is a left adjoint. But by (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Borceux vol. 2
              Thm.5.5.7, p.275) a functor between two locally presentable categories has a left adjoint precisely if it has rank and preserves small limits.
            %p
              Since limits can be constructed from products and equalizers and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
              preserves the latter, it preserves small limits precisely when it preserves small products.
          %h3#RelationToSiteMorphisms Relation to morphisms of (co)sites
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+categories"} small categories
            write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,Set]
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,Set]
            for the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copresheaf"} copresheaf
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} toposes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+categories"} opposite categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^{op}
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sites"} sites
            equipped with the trivial
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+toposes"} sheaf toposes
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              This construction extends to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functor"} 2-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo :
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Cat
                      %mi small
                      %mi co
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Topos
                      %mi ess
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [-,Set] : Cat_{small}^{co} \to Topos_{ess}
            %p
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi small
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_{small}
              with
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topos"} Topos
              on essential geometric morphisms, where a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : C \to D
              is sent to the essential geometric morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                            %mo :
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi Ran
                              %mi f
                        %mover
                          %mo ←
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                            %mo :
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi f
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mo !
                          %mo :
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi Lan
                            %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (f_! \dashv f^* \dashv f_*) :
                    [C,Set]
                    \\stackrel{\overset{f_! := Lan_f}{\to}}{\stackrel{\overset{f^* := (-) \circ f}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{f_* := Ran_f}{\to}}}
                    [D,Set]
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Lan
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lan_f
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ran
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ran_f
              denote the left and right
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
              along
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              This 2-functor is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+2-functor"} full and faithful 2-functor
              when restricted to
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+complete+categories"} Cauchy complete categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo :
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Cat
                      %mi CauchyComp
                      %mi co
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi Topos
                      %mi ess
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [-, Set] : Cat^co_{CauchyComp} \hookrightarrow Topos_{ess}
                    \\,.
            %p
              For all small categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C,D
              we have an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi D
                      %mo ¯
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Topos
                      %mi ess
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Func(\overline{C},\overline{D})^{op}
                    \\simeq
                    Topos_{ess}([C,Set], [D,Set])
            %p
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
              between the
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+completion"} Cauchy completion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              and the the category of essential geometric morphisms between the copresheaf toposes and
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+transformation"} geometric transformation
          %p
            In particular, since every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            – when regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            – is Cauchy complete, we have
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functor"} 2-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo :
                    %mi Poset
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Topos
                      %mi ess
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [-,Set] : Poset \to Topos_{ess}
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+2-functor"} full and faithful 2-functor
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p Sometimes it is useful to decompose this statement as follows.
            %p There is a functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alex
                    %mo :
                    %mi Poset
                    %mo →
                    %mi Locale
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Alex : Poset \to Locale
            %p
              which assigns to each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
              called its
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexandroff+locale"} Alexandroff locale
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              is in the image of this functor precisely if its inverse image morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi Op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* Op(Y) \to Op(X)
              of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Locale"} Locale
            %p
              Moreover, for any poset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Alex
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alex P
              is naturally equivalent to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi P
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [P,Set]
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi Alex
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [-,Set] \simeq Sh \circ Alex
                    \\,.
            %p
              With this, the fact that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo :
                    %mi Poset
                    %mo →
                    %mi Topos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,Set] : Poset \to Topos
              hits precisely the essential geometric morphisms follows with the basic fact about
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+reflection"} localic reflection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo :
                    %mi Locale
                    %mo →
                    %mi Topos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh : Locale \to Topos
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+2-functor"} full and faithful 2-functor
          %h3#some_morphism_calculus Some morphism calculus
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : E \to F
              be an essential geometric morphism.
            %p
              For every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : X \to f^* f_* A
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              the diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi ϕ
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mo !
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\stackrel{\phi}{\to}&amp; f^* f_* A
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    f^* f_! X &amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp; A
                    }
            %p
              commutes, where the vertical morphisms are unit and counit, respectively, and where the bottom horizontal morphism is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              under the composite adjunction
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo !
                      %mo ⊣
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f^* f_! \dashv f^* f_*)
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              The morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : X \to f^* f_* A
              is the component of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi X
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mi ϕ
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo *
                            %mo ↗
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    *&amp;&amp;\overset{X}{\to}&amp;&amp; E
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{A}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;\Downarrow^\phi&amp;&amp; {}^{\mathllap{f^*}}\nearrow
                    \\\
                    E &amp;\underset{f_*}{\to}&amp;F
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              The composite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ϕ
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\phi}{\to}  f^* f_* A \to A
              is the component of this composed with the counit
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi Id
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* f_* \Rightarrow Id
            %p We may insert the 2-identity given by the zig-zag law
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi X
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mi ϕ
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo *
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo !
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots \;\;\; = \;\;\;
                    \\array{
                    *&amp;&amp;\overset{X}{\to}&amp;&amp; E &amp;&amp; = &amp;&amp; E
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{A}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;\Downarrow^\phi&amp;&amp; {}^{\mathllap{f^*}}\nearrow &amp;\Downarrow&amp; \searrow^{f_!}
                    \&amp;\Downarrow&amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{f^*}}
                    \\\
                    E &amp;\underset{f_*}{\to}&amp;F &amp;&amp;=&amp;&amp; F
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Composing this with the counit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi Id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* f_* \Rightarrow Id
              produces the transformation whose component is manifestly the morphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo !
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to f^* f_! X \to A
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#logical_functors_and_etale_geometric_morphisms Logical functors and etale geometric morphisms
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logical+functor"} logical functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\to F
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            has automatically also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            whence is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
            part of an essential geometric morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\to E
          %p A particularly important instance of this situation is the following:
          %p
            For any morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon A\to B
            in a topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon E/A \to E/B
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*:E/B\to E/A
            of course.
          %p
            In the special case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo =
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B = *
            the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi : E/A \to E
          %p
            is also called an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+geometric+morphism"} etale geometric morphism
          %p
            Conversely, (almost) any essential geometric morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi^*
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logical+functor"} logical functor
            has the form of an
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+geometric+morphism"} etale geometric morphism
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              If the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_!
              of a logical functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi π
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi^*:E\to F
              furthermore preserves equalizers, then the corresponding essential geometric morphism is up to equivalence an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+geometric+morphism"} etale geometric morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo :
                    %mi F
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi : F\simeq E/A \to E
              for an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              that is determined up to isomorphism.
          %p
            For a proof see e.g. Johnstone
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#JTT77"} (1977, p.37)
          %h3#locally_connected_toposes Locally connected toposes
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topos"} locally connected topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is one where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma : E \to Set
            is essential.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi E
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Γ
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi LConst
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mn 0
                  %mi Set
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (f_! \dashv f^* \dashv f_*) \;\;\; : \;\;\;
                  E
                  \\stackrel{\overset{\Pi_0}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{LConst}{\longleftarrow}}{\underset{\Gamma}{\longrightarrow}}}
                  Set
                  \\,.
          %p
            In this case, the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo !
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_! = \Pi_0 : E \to Set
            sends each object to its set of connected components. More on this situation is at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} homotopy groups in an (∞,1)-topos
          %p
            Note, though that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon E\to S
            is an arbitrary geometric morphism through which we regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            as an
            = succeed "-topos," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed ",\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            to be locally connected as an
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is essential, but that the left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_!
            can be made into an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+functor"} indexed functor
            (which is automatically true for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^*
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_*
            = succeed "-toposes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundation"} foundation
            is
            = succeed "\u2014and" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/material+set+theory"} material set theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structural+set+theory"} structural set theory
            = succeed "-indexed" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+geometric+morphism"} locally connected geometric morphism
          %h3#tiny_objects Tiny objects
          %p
            The
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tiny+object"} tiny object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,Set]
            are precisely the essential points
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set \to [C,Set]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tiny+object"} tiny object
            for details.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+subtopos"} essential subtopos
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/level+of+a+topos"} level of a topos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topos"} locally connected topos
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} locally ∞-connected (∞,1)-topos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topos"} connected topos
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} ∞-connected (∞,1)-topos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/totally+connected+topos"} totally connected topos
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/totally+connected+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} totally connected (∞,1)-topos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+topos"} local topos
                \/
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} local (∞,1)-topos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
          %h2#references References
          %p Like many other things, it all started as an exercise in
          %ul
            %li#SGA4
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M.+Artin"}> M. Artin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A.+Grothendieck"} A. Grothendieck
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+L.+Verdier"} J. L. Verdier
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Théorie des Topos et Cohomologie Etale des Schémas (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SGA4"}> SGA4
                  )
              %strong 269
              Springer Heidelberg 1972. (exposé IV, ex.7.6, pp.414-417)
          %p
            Speaking of exercises, consider the results of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Erik+Roos"} Roos
            on essential points reported in exercise 7.3 of
          %ul
            %li#JTT77
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              ,
              %em Topos Theory
              , Academic Press New York 1977. (Dover reprint 2014, pp.254f)
          %p
            The case of sheaves valued in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
            is considered in
          %ul
            %li
              J. Haigh,
              %em Essential geometric morphisms between toposes of finite sets
              , Math. Proc. Phil. Soc.
              %strong 87
              (1980) pp.21-24.
          %p
            The standard reference for
            %em essential localizations
            = succeed "," do
              %sup#fnref:1
                %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/level+of+a+topos"} levels
          %ul
            %li#KL89
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G.+M.+Kelly"}> G. M. Kelly
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F.+W.+Lawvere"} F. W. Lawvere
              %em On the Complete Lattice of Essential Localizations
              , Bull. Soc. Math. de Belgique
              %strong XLI
              (1989) 289-319 &amp;lbrack;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Kelly-Lawvere_EssentialLocalizations.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p For more on this see also
          %ul
            %li#Lima15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Guilherme+Frederico+Lima"}> Guilherme Frederico Lima
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em From Essential Inclusions to Local Geometric Morphisms
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/747/"} Topos à l’IHES
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YsoGN91Rh_s"} video
          %p The definition of essential geometric morphisms appears before Lemma A.4.1.5 in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+Elephant"} Sketches of an Elephant
                vol. I
              , Oxford UP 2002.
          %p Connected surjective and local geometric morphisms are discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              %em Local maps of toposes
              , Proceedings London Mathematical Society
              %strong 58
              (1989), pp.281-305.
          %p Further refinements are in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bill+Lawvere"}> Bill Lawvere
              ,
              %em Axiomatic cohesion
              Theory and Applications of Categories, Vol. 19, No. 3, 2007, pp. 41–49. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/19/3/19-03.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          .footnotes
            %hr/
            %ol
              %li#fn:1
                %p
                  See at
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aufhebung"} Aufhebung
                  for further references on essential localizations.
                  %a{:href => "#fnref:1", :rev => "footnote"} ↩
